"}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Weather and Seasons"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The weather is what it feels like outside. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">It's </span>... with an adjective (describing word), to talk about the weather."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Seasons are a period of the year. Seasons in the Northern Hemisphere include:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":\"05\",\"columns\":\"02\",\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Season </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Months </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Summer\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"June, July, August\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Fall\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"September, October, November\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Winter\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"December, January, February\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Spring\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"March, April, May\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Tom </span>:      What's the weather like in winter?<br /> <span class=\"strong\">Susan </span>:      It's cold."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Tom </span>:      Is the weather cold in spring?<br /> <span class=\"strong\">Susan </span>:      No. It's cool and it rains."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Tom </span>:      What's the weather like in summer?<br /> <span class=\"strong\">Susan </span>:      It's hot!"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Nouns and Adjectives <br /> Relating to the Weather\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Examples\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"hot\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's so hot!\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"temperature\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The temperature is just right.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's a perfect day.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"nice\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's a nice day.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"sunny\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's sunny too!\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Free Time Activities "}, {"type": "describer", "content": " "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the Simple Present tense to talk about free time activities. You do free time activities when you are relaxed. You don't do free time activities when you work."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I go to the gym. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You play the guitar."}, {"type": "example", "content": "He plays volleyball. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We take Japanese classes."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The children make model airplanes. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hot "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "high temperature "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's so hot! Let's go to the beach! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le02ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about the weather."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "temperature "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the measurement of heat or cold "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The temperature is just right. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le02ob03aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "beautiful "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "great; amazing (weather) "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's a beautiful day today.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le02ob03aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sun "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the source of heat for our world "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The sun is shining."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le02ob03aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sunny "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "when the sun is shining "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It is nice and sunny outside."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le02ob03aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to go for a walk "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "put one foot in front of the other "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We can go for a walk."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le02ob03aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to stay home "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to not go out "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I prefer to stay home tonight."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le02ob03aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to go swimming "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to exercise by moving in water "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Do you want to go swimming or play volleyball?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le02ob03aud08"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn2le02ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go on the Internet or look in the newspaper. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find out what the weather is like today in 3 different cities."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 3 sentences about the weather in each city."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your sentences to a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write about the weather in different cities."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use words about the weather."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about about the weather."}]}], "type": "sena"}